Let the 2 roots be  $a$  and  $b$ . Notice that the sum of the squares of the roots can be expressed as  $(a+b)^2-2ab$ . Using Vieta's Formulas,  $a+b=-2h$  and  $ab=-3$ . Substituting those gets 

\begin{align*} (a+b)^2-2ab&=10 \Rightarrow\quad 4h^2+6&=10 \Rightarrow\quad h^2&=1 \Rightarrow\quad |h|=1 \end{align*}

The answer is, therefore:  $\textbf{(E) }\text{None of these} $

